morse-fgh100m-dkms (1.16.4-3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Detect the 5-arg cfg80211_port_authorized() by probing the target
    kernel headers: newer Rockchip vendor 6.1 trees (still reporting
    LINUX_VERSION_CODE 6.1.172) backported the td_bitmap/td_bitmap_len
    parameters without bumping MAC80211_VERSION_CODE, so the existing
    version guards picked the removed 3-arg call and the build failed
    with "too few arguments to function 'cfg80211_port_authorized'"

 -- Seeed Studio <techsupport@seeed.cc>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0800

morse-fgh100m-dkms (1.16.4-2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Extend the IEEE80211_CHAN_IGNORE compat shim to aarch64: the stock
    shim (mapping to IEEE80211_CHAN_DISABLED on unpatched kernels) only
    guarded __x86_64__, leaving arm64 builds against vendor 6.1 headers
    with an undeclared identifier
  * Add BUILT_MODULE_LOCATION to dkms.conf: the modules are built under
    src/ and src/dot11ah/, but DKMS only checked the build root and
    failed with "Build of morse.ko failed" after a successful make

 -- Seeed Studio <techsupport@seeed.cc>  Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0800

